## Communications
## Metal–Organic Frameworks
Counterintuitive crystallization kinetics are uncovered in the metal–organic framework ZIF-8, using in situ XRD and pH measurements. The findings are explained by a pre-equilibrium model in which metastable, over-stoichiometric species inhibit crystallization. The model helps to rationalize apparent contradictions between previous studies and opens up new opportunities for crystallization control in network solids.
